Package: mscc
Version: 1.0.72
Section: hamradio
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Multus SDR / MSCC Linux <local@localhost>
Installed-Size: 1350
Depends: libc6, libportaudio2, libusb-1.0-0, libhidapi-libusb0, build-essential, kmod, udev, passwd, alsa-utils, pulseaudio-utils, python3, python3-tk, stlink-tools, dfu-util, python3-usb, usbutils
Conflicts: proficio-flash-tools
Replaces: proficio-flash-tools
Recommends: linux-headers-rpi-v8 | linux-headers-rpi-2712, pipewire-pulse | pulseaudio, pipewire, libnotify-bin, python3-pyaudio
Homepage: https://local/mscc
Description: MSCC stack for Multus/Proficio on Raspberry Pi OS (64-bit)
 Prebuilt MSCC servers (ms-sdr, sdrcore-recv, sdrcore-trans),
 Proficio PSoC firmware upload (psoc-bootloader CLI + psoc-bootloader.gui), start/stop script,
 Pulse/PipeWire virtual digi sinks (VirtualA/B), desktop menu
 Start/Stop/Status/Firmware Upload, and tty0tty null-modem module.
 Black Pill (STM32F411) flash tools: stm32-app-flash <file.bin> (USB DFU)
 and stm32-bootloader-flash <file.bin> (ST-Link); replaces the old
 proficio-flash-tools package.
 Includes NFM (MODE_FM) RX/TX and CMD_SET_FM_POWER (0x9E) when binaries
 are rebuilt from SDRcore-*-linux / ms-sdr-linux with FM sources.
 .
 Supported platform: Raspberry Pi OS 64-bit on Pi 4 / Pi 5 only.
 Not intended for other Linux distributions.
 .
 Installs binaries into the installing user's $HOME/mscc, seeds
 $HOME/.local/mscc only when missing/empty, creates /usr/local/bin
 links, enables user service mscc-virtual-audio, and builds/loads tty0tty.
 .
 Desktop menu: MSCC Start / MSCC Stop / MSCC Status (mscc-desktop-ctl).
 mscc status: servers plus config, PortAudio device match, CAT, digi sinks.
 Digi path: VirtualA (recv out) / VirtualB.monitor (trans digi mic).
 Servers need Pulse-capable PortAudio from
 mscc-portaudio at /usr/local (rpath + ldconfig) to list Virtual*.
 .
 Kernel headers (linux-headers-rpi-v8 or rpi-2712) needed for tty0tty.
 python3-pyaudio recommended so status can list PortAudio devices.
